WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.017 --> 00:00:02.869
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.202
- It's punching.

00:00:05.139 --> 00:00:06.222
It's kicking.

00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:11.469
Armored combat is sort of
like, uh, MMA, but with weapons.

00:00:11.469 --> 00:00:14.886
To me, this is the ultimate combat sport.

00:00:19.728 --> 00:00:21.880
My name is Andre Sinou,
I'm the co-founder of

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.686
the Armored Combat League.

00:00:23.686 --> 00:00:26.536
I'm the captain of the
national sword fighting team,

00:00:26.536 --> 00:00:27.869
the USA Knights.

00:00:28.847 --> 00:00:32.247
Our form of armored combat started

00:00:32.247 --> 00:00:33.967
a little over four years ago.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:36.349
It came to our ears that
there were some people

00:00:36.349 --> 00:00:38.160
over in Europe that were doing this

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.088
and we had to build a United States team

00:00:40.088 --> 00:00:42.728
and try to be competitive with the world.

00:00:42.728 --> 00:00:45.280
Most of the arms and armor that we use

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:49.128
comes from the late 14th
and early 15th century,

00:00:49.128 --> 00:00:50.406
Western Europe.

00:00:50.406 --> 00:00:54.248
Now there's some other armors
but the best bang for the buck

00:00:54.248 --> 00:00:58.415
is usually late 14th century,
early 15th century armor.

00:01:01.288 --> 00:01:02.819
It's kinda counterintuitive,
but if you're wearing

00:01:02.819 --> 00:01:04.520
decent armor and you get hit with a sword,

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.617
half the time you don't
even know you've been hit.

00:01:06.617 --> 00:01:08.688
(clanking)

00:01:08.688 --> 00:01:12.750
If you played football,
you've done a rougher thing.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:15.301
It's a brawl, I mean
there's no doubt about it,

00:01:15.301 --> 00:01:16.669
you're going out there
and you're brawling.

00:01:16.669 --> 00:01:18.160
Just like in rugby or football,

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.731
you've got to have a plan
when you go out there.

00:01:20.731 --> 00:01:23.400
The flankers end up with
three people on them

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.211
and you end up with two.

00:01:25.211 --> 00:01:27.800
Now melees are a lot more intense.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:30.989
Those rules are, you
fight until submission,

00:01:30.989 --> 00:01:34.524
or until you put somebody
down to the ground.

00:01:34.524 --> 00:01:36.931
(banging)

00:01:36.931 --> 00:01:38.999
There's no typical person
for armored combat.

00:01:38.999 --> 00:01:42.011
You've got people from all walks of life,

00:01:42.011 --> 00:01:43.608
whether it's some sort of martial arts

00:01:43.608 --> 00:01:48.105
or football or rugby, there's
some history buffs too.

00:01:48.105 --> 00:01:50.361
And they'll fight and fight and fight,

00:01:50.361 --> 00:01:53.841
and they'll give everything,
to the point of exhaustion.

00:01:53.841 --> 00:01:55.601
That's what makes a winner.

00:01:55.601 --> 00:01:56.768
It's all here.

00:01:57.635 --> 00:02:00.744
These guys will go hard at each other.

00:02:00.744 --> 00:02:02.772
They're gonna be swinging
as hard as they can.

00:02:02.772 --> 00:02:04.572
They're trying to knock you down,

00:02:04.572 --> 00:02:06.292
they're trying to get you to submit,

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:07.845
and then they're gonna help you up,

00:02:07.845 --> 00:02:08.932
they're gonna pat you on the back,

00:02:08.932 --> 00:02:13.099
and they're gonna go have a
steak and a beer with you.

